docs/schwab-api-contract.md:5:Hosts: `https://api.schwabapi.com/trader/v1` and `https://api.schwabapi.com/marketdata/v1`. Every API call sends `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` and `Accept: application/json`. Responses are bare arrays or objects, no envelope.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:25:| `Schwab::ReauthRequired < AuthError` | any token-endpoint 4xx (`invalid_client`, `invalid_grant`, `refresh_token_authentication_error`, `unsupported_token_type`); the pause path |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:28:| `Schwab::RequestError` | 400, 403, 404; never retried; a 400 on `startDate` is how the lookback cap announces itself |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:33:Error bodies: API errors are JSON:API style `{"errors":[{"id","status","title","detail","source"}]}`; the token endpoint uses `{"error","error_description"}`; gateway 401s and 5xxs can be non-JSON. The parser tolerates all three.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:41:| Token endpoint | `POST /v1/oauth/token`, `Authorization: Basic base64("#{app_key}:#{app_secret}")`, `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:43:| Refresh grant | `grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={token}` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:44:| Token response | `{"expires_in":1800,"token_type":"Bearer","scope":"api","refresh_token","access_token","id_token"}`; `id_token` is not persisted |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:45:| Access token | 30 minutes; expired tokens are rejected outright (API 401) |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:46:| Refresh token | 7 days from the authorization-code grant. **Refreshing does not extend it.** `refresh_expires_at` is set once at issuance and never moved |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:47:| Refresh response | includes a `refresh_token`; store whatever comes back, keep `refresh_expires_at` |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:49:The refresh job runs every 25 minutes. A token-endpoint 4xx is `ReauthRequired`: no backoff, no retry, pause sync.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:79:**Also `GET /accounts/{hash}/orders/{orderId}`** for one order. Known working stops older than the lookback are re-fetched by id, otherwise positions get falsely flagged unprotected.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:107:  "type", "status": VALID|INVALID|PENDING|UNKNOWN, "subAccount": CASH|MARGIN|SHORT|DIV|INCOME|UNKNOWN,
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:119:One date per call, today to one year out. Open day: `{"equity":{"EQ":{"date","marketType","product","isOpen":true,"sessionHours":{"preMarket":[{"start","end"}],"regularMarket":[...],"postMarket":[...]}}}}` with `-04:00` offsets. Closed day (TD-era behavior, unverified): key changes from `EQ` to `equity`, `sessionHours` absent, `isOpen` false. The mapper takes the first value under `equity` regardless of key, treats missing `sessionHours` as closed, and uses min start and max end per session. Early closes show as a shorter `regularMarket` interval.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:134:| Orders and transactions lookback | 60 days, one constant | Schwabdev says one year; probe 61+ days on approval |
