docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:14:2. Schwab OAuth (three-legged) and the full token lifecycle from §5.1: 25-minute access refresh job, 7-day refresh-token expiry tracking, `submission_unknown` and reconciliation are Phase 2 but design the `orders` table for them now.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:18:6. Dashboard with all four banner states (healthy / token expiring / token expired / halted). Halted can be reached via a manual flag in Phase 1 since no guardrails run yet.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:20:8. Scheduled runtime (§5.5a): Solid Queue jobs calling the Anthropic Messages API with read-only tool definitions, hard tool-turn cap, email output. Implement the 07:00 brief and 16:30 EOD; Sunday review can be a stub that emails the re-auth link and token age.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:28:- **No live Schwab calls in tests.** VCR/WebMock cassettes only, scrubbed of tokens and encrypted account values. A `FakeSchwab` adapter backs Playwright and dev seeds.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:32:- **Every "logged" action is an `audit_events` row.** Re-auth, token refresh failures, shadow-mode toggles, manual halt flag.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:38:- RSpec full suite. Priority order from PRD §5.11: token lifecycle with time travel, sync jobs with fixture payloads including dividends and corporate actions, journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fills, ticker change on the same CUSIP), MCP tool contracts.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:47:2. Build vertically: migrations → Schwab adapter with cassettes → OAuth + token jobs → sync jobs → journal builder → dashboard → MCP → scheduled runtime. Green `bin/ci` at each step.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:35:└─────────────┘                      │  - OAuth token lifecycle  │
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:49:**Why Rails and not just an agent:** the agent cannot be trusted with credentials, token refresh timing, idempotent order submission, or rule enforcement. Those are deterministic jobs. The agent is good at synthesis, briefs, screening, and post-mortems. Split accordingly.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:58:- **OAuth:** three-legged OAuth 2.0. Access token ~30 min, refresh token hard-expires at 7 days with no programmatic renewal.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:59:  - Background job refreshes the access token every ~25 minutes while a valid refresh token exists.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:60:  - Re-auth flow: when the refresh token is within 24h of expiry, the app notifies (email/SMS/push) with a one-click link to redo the browser login. Track refresh-token age as a first-class health metric on the dashboard.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:61:  - All scheduled work checks token health first and degrades gracefully (queues, does not silently skip).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:64:- **Secrets:** app key/secret in Rails credentials; tokens encrypted at rest (Active Record Encryption). Nothing broker-related in the memory files repo.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:136:- If the bracket child fails to place after the parent fills, the position is flagged `unprotected` on the dashboard and in a push/email immediately; this is a hard alert, not a brief item.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:137:- Working stops are reconciled against Schwab on every orders sync; a stop that disappears at the broker (cancelled out-of-band) flags the position `unprotected`.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:143:- `get_account_health` (equity, settled cash, drawdown, token status)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:153:Explicitly absent from MCP: submit_order, cancel_order, edit_risk_rules, token operations. Submission happens only in the Rails approval UI (or a signed confirmation link), by the human.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:159:- **Interactive (human present):** the Claude app (desktop/Cowork/web) with the Rails MCP server registered as a remote connector. Rails exposes MCP over HTTPS with bearer-token auth (token in dokku config, rotatable). This is where ad hoc analysis, screening, and order proposals happen, billed through the Claude subscription seat.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:160:- **Scheduled (unattended):** Solid Queue jobs on the VPS call the Anthropic Messages API directly with an API key, passing tool definitions that map to the same internal service layer the MCP server uses (in-process, no MCP hop). Output is rendered to email. This covers the 07:00 brief, 16:30 EOD, and Sunday review. **Unattended runs get read-only tools only.** These runs ingest untrusted text (transcripts, news, fetched pages), so `propose_order`, `add_watchlist_item`, and `annotate_trade` are not in their tool set; anything a brief wants to suggest is rendered as text in the email, and the human creates the proposal interactively. Write tools exist only in the interactive runtime. Each scheduled job also has a hard cap on tool turns. Rationale: unattended runs can't depend on a desktop app being open, and keeping the scheduler in Rails means the VPS is the single ops surface (one place for cron, retries, failure alerts, and the token-health gate).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:176:- 07:00 ET pre-market brief: overnight moves on holdings/watchlist, gaps, today's earnings/econ events touching the book, stops at risk, settled-cash status. Delivered by email.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:179:- Token-health nag when refresh token < 24h from expiry.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:197:- **Notifications, revised:** time-sensitive alerts move from email to push once the app exists: new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, `unprotected` position, token expiring. Briefs and the Sunday ritual stay email (long-form, read on a desktop anyway). Push payloads carry no financial figures; they deep-link and the app fetches.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:199:- **Auth to the Rails app:** the native shell holds a session like the browser does; no separate API auth. The MCP bearer token is never on the phone.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:207:- Schwab app key/secret in dokku config vars; tokens encrypted at rest in Postgres.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:213:The 7-day refresh token becomes a scheduled habit instead of a surprise:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:215:- Sunday evening email bundles: (a) the weekly edge review, (b) a re-auth link to redo the Schwab browser login, (c) system health summary (last sync times, job failures, token age).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:216:- Re-authing every Sunday resets the 7-day clock so it never expires mid-week. Caveat: expiry is 7 days from issuance, so the email lands earlier than the prior week's auth time, and a daily health check escalates (Mon, then Tue) if the re-auth hasn't happened. On expiry, sync jobs pause and queue rather than erroring.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:224:  4. Schwab client service layer: VCR/WebMock cassettes only. The suite never touches the live API; cassettes get scrubbed of tokens and encrypted account values before commit.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:251:**Phase 1 (read-only):** Schwab OAuth + token lifecycle, account/position/transaction sync, dashboard, journal auto-population from fills, memory repo, MCP read tools, daily briefs.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:296:- **7-day refresh token** is the top operational risk; a missed re-auth silently kills all automation. Mitigated by health checks and nags, but it cannot be engineered away.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:300:- Unprotected positions: bracket child failing to place or being cancelled out-of-band. Mitigated by immediate hard alert and per-sync reconciliation (5.4.2).
